      "body": "## Overview\n\nExplain the implicit reasoning-end masking introduced in #61574, following the [documentation request](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/61574#pullrequestreview-5543234444).\n\n## Claims\n\n- Clarify the exception to `enable_in_reasoning=False`: engine-based parsers mask single-token implicit ends that cannot start the request's grammar.\n- Explain that grammar-valid implicit ends, explicit reasoning ends and other reasoning tokens remain allowed by this reasoning-phase mask.\n\n## Validation\n\nApplicable pre-commit hooks passed, including markdownlint and typos. Checked the wording against the current manager, parser and configuration defaults, then ran the existing behavior tests:\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest \\\n  tests/v1/structured_output/test_structured_output_manager.py \\\n  tests/parser/engine/test_parser_engine.py \\\n  -k 'reasoning_rows_mask_grammar_invalid_implicit_end or parallel_fill_masks_grammar_invalid_implicit_end or initial_constraint_activation or TestReasoningEndTokenIds' \\\n  -v --tb=short\n```\n\n21 passed, 168 deselected. These check existing runtime behavior; no runtime code or tests are changed. A full MkDocs site build was not run.\n\n## Details\n\nChecked 25 open documentation-overlap PRs at their current heads. #58219 covers token-ID versus rendered-text boundaries; #59967 covers Qwen3 implicit tool-call endings. Neither documents this grammar-invalid boundary mask. AI assistance was used for research, wording and validation.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
